<title>GERMANY: Dresdner says lost 4 mln dmk through rogue trader.</title>
<headline>Dresdner says lost 4 mln dmk through rogue trader.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dresdner Bank AG said on Monday it lost four million marks ($2.6 million) as a result of false accounting by a trader in its bond dealing department.</p>
<p>A spokesman for the bank said its internal risk controls had discovered a discrepancy at the end of August and the dealer had been dismissed without notice.</p>
<p>The trader had conducted false accounting in his trading book, possibly to present better trading profits, the spokesman said.</p>
<p>It was not immediately clear whether police were investigating the incident.</p>
<p>&quot;The bank is proud that its control systems worked so well and that the manipulation was discovered in a very short space of time,&quot; the spokesman said.</p>
<p>--David Crossland, Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525 ($ = 1.542 German Marks)</p>
</text>
